# The village by the pond. Knot names are global; NPCs point at them with
# LevelSpawn.dialogue. See sim/dialogue/sim_dialogue.gd for the format.

=== merchant
{self.suspicious} Merchant: Keep your hands where I can see them, friend.
{quest.bandits.cleared and not merchant_paid} -> merchant_reward
{quest.bandits.cleared and merchant_paid} Merchant: Carts on the west road again. Thank you, truly.
{quest.bandits.cleared} -> END
{not bandits_known} Merchant: Travellers! Off a boat, and not the road? Then you were lucky.
{bandits_known} Merchant: Any news about the camp on the hill?
* {not bandits_known} [Lucky how?] -> merchant_bandits
* {bandits_known} [Tell me about the bandits again.] -> merchant_bandits
* {self.suspicious and not merchant_calmed and talker.charisma >= 2} [(Charisma) A misunderstanding. We're on your side.] -> merchant_calm
* [Let's trade.] -> merchant_trade
* [What do you sell?] -> merchant_goods
* [Goodbye.] -> END

=== merchant_bandits
Merchant: Bandits took the old camp past the forest, west along the road. Six of them, maybe more.
Merchant: They stop every cart. The guard won't go up alone, and I don't blame him.
~ bandits_known = 1
Merchant: Clear them out and I'll make it worth your while. I've a silver ring put by.
* [We'll deal with them.] -> merchant_promise
* [Not our problem.] -> merchant_refuse

=== merchant_promise
~ bandits_promised = 1
Merchant: Gods bless you. Mind the one with the fire, he's mad.
-> END

=== merchant_refuse
Merchant: No. No, I suppose it isn't.
-> END

=== merchant_calm
~ merchant_calmed = 1
~ calm
Merchant: ...Fine. Fine. Bandits on the road, everyone's jumpy. Forget it.
-> merchant

=== merchant_goods
{self.has.Map} Merchant: Bread, rope, and a map of these roads, if you've coin. Nobody has coin, with the road shut.
{not self.has.Map} Merchant: I had a map of the roads... it's gone. Funny, that.
-> merchant

=== merchant_trade
{self.suspicious} Merchant: Coin first. I've learned that much.
{not self.suspicious} Merchant: Have a look. Prices are fair, mostly.
~ trade
-> END

=== merchant_reward
Merchant: You did it? The camp is empty? Then here, as I promised.
{self.has.Silver_ring} ~ give Silver ring
{has.Silver_ring} Merchant: Wear it well.
{not has.Silver_ring} Merchant: I had a ring for you. Someone's had it off me. I'm sorry, truly.
~ merchant_paid = 1
-> END

=== guard
{self.suspicious} Guard: I've got my eye on you. One wrong move.
{quest.bandits.cleared} Guard: The camp's quiet. Didn't think anyone could do it.
{quest.bandits.cleared} -> END
Guard: Move along. And stay off the west road unless you want a knife in you.
* [Why don't you deal with the bandits?] -> guard_bandits
* {self.suspicious and not guard_calmed and talker.charisma >= 2} [(Charisma) You've the wrong people, guard.] -> guard_calm
* {talker.historian >= 1 and not guard_lore} [(Historian) That camp was a toll post once, wasn't it?] -> guard_lore
* {smuggler_known and not smuggler_reported and not quest.smuggler.done} [There's a smuggler on the north-west shore.] -> guard_smuggler
* [Fine.] -> END

=== guard_calm
~ guard_calmed = 1
~ calm
Guard: ...Maybe. Maybe I have. Don't make me regret it.
-> END

=== guard_lore
~ guard_lore = 1
Guard: Aye, the old toll post. Before the road went bad. You know your history.
Guard: Built on the rise so you see the whole road from it. Mind the high ground up there.
-> END

=== guard_bandits
Guard: One spear against six? I'd be dead by noon and the village would have no guard at all.
Guard: Their chief keeps the camp key on him. Whatever they've taken is in his chest.
~ bandits_known = 1
-> END

=== guard_smuggler
~ smuggler_reported = 1
Guard: On the old shore? I wondered how the tavern always has wine with the road shut.
{talker.has.Sealed_package} Guard: And that's his, is it? I'll take it. Evidence.
{talker.has.Sealed_package} ~ take Sealed package
Guard: I'll see to him. There's a reward for honest folk, when the captain remembers to pay it.
-> END

=== villager
{quest.bandits.cleared} Villager: They say the camp is empty! Is it true?
{quest.bandits.cleared} -> END
Villager: Don't go up the hill. Please.
-> END

=== farmer
{self.suspicious} Farmer: You again. Watch yourself.
{quest.granary.saved} Farmer: The barn stands. I keep walking out to look at it. Thank you.
{quest.granary.saved} -> END
{quest.granary.burned} Farmer: All of it. The whole winter's grain. Don't talk to me.
{quest.granary.burned} -> END
Farmer: Ruffians are squatting by my barn on the west road. They said if I come back they'll burn it, with the lamp oil I keep there.
~ granary_warned = 1
* [We'll run them off.] -> farmer_promise
* [Anything else wrong around here?] -> farmer_shepherd
* [Not our business.] -> END

=== farmer_promise
Farmer: Mind the oil barrel by the door. One spark and the barn goes up, and the grain with it.
-> END

=== farmer_shepherd
Farmer: Old Hob took his flock up into the southern hills a week ago. The flock came back without him.
~ shepherd_known = 1
Farmer: More of those ruffians up there, I'd wager.
-> END

=== smith
{self.suspicious} Smith: I've nothing for thieves.
{quest.hammer.returned} Smith: Listen to that ring. Best sound in the world. Thank you again.
{quest.hammer.returned} -> END
{talker.has.Forge_hammer} -> smith_return
Smith: Can't work. Some quick-fingered bandit lifted my forge hammer off the bench in broad daylight.
~ hammer_known = 1
Smith: Thin fellow, ran west towards the camp. Bring it back and you'll not leave empty-handed.
* [We'll keep an eye out.] -> END
* [What will you give us?] -> smith_reward_ask

=== smith_reward_ask
Smith: A helm I finished last month. Good iron. Better on your head than on my shelf.
-> END

=== smith_return
Smith: That's it! That's my hammer! Where did you...? Never mind. Never mind!
~ take Forge hammer
~ hammer_returned = 1
{self.has.Iron_helm} ~ give Iron helm
{self.has.Iron_helm} Smith: Here. You've earned it.
{not self.has.Iron_helm} Smith: I'd have given you the helm... it's gone from the shelf. Strange days.
-> END

=== tavern
{self.suspicious} Marta: Drink up and go.
Marta: Welcome to the Drowned Lantern. Nothing's coming up the road, so it's cider or nothing.
* [Heard anything interesting?] -> tavern_gossip
* {talker.has.Sealed_package} [A man on the north-west shore sent this.] -> tavern_package
* [Let's trade.] -> tavern_trade
* [Goodbye.] -> END

=== tavern_gossip
{not hammer_known} Marta: The smith's in a black mood. Someone took his hammer.
{not shepherd_known} Marta: Old Hob the shepherd never came down from the southern hills.
{not shepherd_known} ~ shepherd_known = 1
Marta: There's an old mine in the northern hills, below the cliffs. Shut since the roof fell in. Children say there's treasure. Children say a lot.
Marta: And someone's hidden a chest out past the pond, west of here. Every drunk in this village has looked for it.
* {talker.charisma >= 1} [(Charisma) You know everyone. Who brings your wine, with the road shut?] -> tavern_wine
* [Thanks.] -> END

=== tavern_wine
Marta: ...A friend. On the old shore, north-west, where the wrecks wash up. Don't go bothering him.
~ smuggler_known = 1
-> END

=== tavern_package
Marta: Not here! ...Give it. Quickly.
~ take Sealed package
~ package_delivered = 1
{self.has.Gold} ~ give Gold
Marta: That's for your trouble. And you never saw me take it.
-> END

=== tavern_trade
Marta: Cider, bread, and whatever's left.
~ trade
-> END
